[38;5;231m⏺[39m I added a basic checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m. Ticking it marks the item as done, and unticking it puts it back.

  - It's a native [38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m inside a [38;5;153m<label>[39m, so you can click the text as well as the box. It also works
    with the keyboard.
  - When it's checked, a small CSS rule crosses out the item's text and greys it out. Delete the [38;5;153m<style>[39m block if you
    only want the box.
  - There's no JavaScript. The browser tracks whether it's on or off, so the state resets when the page reloads.

  I haven't opened it in a browser. To add more items, copy the [38;5;153m<label class="task">…</label>[39m block. If you want items
  to stay checked after a reload or be added from a list, that needs a little JavaScript, which I can add.

